# SF109: the game-over screen's new look gets the household language and its result tones
#
# Intent: the shared game-over screen (UX15d) is built in the household's language (six languages) instead of the two the games had, and plays its result tone table
#   when the new look is on. Look 0 (today's screen and sounds) is unchanged, and the look stays off by default.
# Placement: body (the unit's own screen and speaker); no brain half needed, the language is the unit's own setting.
# Upstream: none (MaiPai code only).
# Check after a flash: bench train game-over-look: look 0 is pixel-identical to before; look 1 shows the localized text and plays the tones silently at volume 0.
# Kconfig: none (rides on the existing game-over look switch, bench only).
# Memory cost: a short-lived PSRAM buffer (under 40 KB) while a tone table plays, freed straight after; nothing while the look is off.

